@@ -51,3 +51,23 @@ applyPatch({ users: ['Ada'] }, [
   { op: 'add', path: '/users/-', value: 'Grace' },
 ]); // { users: ['Ada', 'Grace'] }
 ```
+
+## JSON Merge Patch
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies an [RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
+and returns a new document. When the patch is an object, its non-null members are merged recursively;
+members assigned `null` are removed. A non-object patch replaces the target, including arrays, which
+are never merged element-by-element. If an object patch is applied to a non-object target, the target
+is treated as an empty object.
+
+Both inputs must contain JSON values: finite numbers, strings, booleans, `null`, dense arrays, and
+plain objects. The function rejects JavaScript-only values and never mutates either input.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+applyMergePatch(
+  { profile: { name: 'Ada', title: 'Engineer' } },
+  { profile: { title: null, team: 'Research' } },
+); // { profile: { name: 'Ada', team: 'Research' } }
+```
