+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-005-keep-json-merge-patch-inputs-json-only-and-immutable.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+---
+id: dl-005-keep-json-merge-patch-inputs-json-only-and-immutable
+type: decision-log
+title: "Keep JSON Merge Patch inputs JSON-only and immutable"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 7386 operates on JSON values, while this TypeScript library receives JavaScript values at its
+public API boundary. `applyPatch` already rejects values that JSON cannot represent and returns an
+independent result. Merge Patch needs the same boundary behaviour so callers can safely use both
+update APIs interchangeably.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate and deep-clone both the target and patch as JSON values before applying the RFC 7386 merge
+algorithm. Reject JavaScript-only values, including sparse arrays, non-finite numbers, cycles and
+non-plain objects. Mutate only the cloned target during recursive object merging; return a cloned
+patch value for a non-object replacement.
+
+## Consequences
+
+`applyMergePatch` preserves both input values on success and errors before producing a result for
+invalid input. Its API accepts the same JSON value subset as `applyPatch`, while its merge semantics
+remain those defined by RFC 7386.
